   "notes": "The ambient row transcribes Section 2 paragraph 5: Archimedes bulk density 3.566(5) g/cm^3 and ambient VP=9.74(1), VS=6.00(1) km/s; unavailable moduli and pressure fields remain blank rather than being inferred. The other rows are a lossless field-wise transcription of the official publisher Table 1 file. The first seven high-pressure rows are the initial room-temperature compression. The remaining ten are decompression measurements collected at room temperature after annealing at up to 800 degC. Pcal is calculated from the acoustic-derived BM3 and must not be treated as an independent pressure observation for a volumetric refit. The fourth initial-compression row is retained exactly as printed even though its V/V0=0.962 is internally inconsistent with its density and Pcal columns. The Table 1 footnote reports the conventional-cell reference V0=74.702(26) A^3 separately; it is stored on the EOS record rather than duplicated as a synthetic data row."
